<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20578] sanity-lnet check_parameter() assumes every interface is configured</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20578</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;check_parameter() in lustre/tests/sanity-lnet.sh compares the number of NIs reporting a tunable against ${#INTERFACES&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;@&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;}:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;check_parameter() {
	local para=$1
	local value=$2

	echo &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"check parameter ${para} value ${value}"&lt;/span&gt;

	&lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; $(( $(do_lnetctl net show -v | \
		     tee /dev/stderr | \
		     grep -c &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"^ \+${para}: ${value}$"&lt;/span&gt;) != ${#INTERFACES[@]} ))
}
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_241 configures only INTERFACES&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;0&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;, so on any node with two or more LNet interfaces the count is 1 while ${#INTERFACES&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;@&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;} is 2 or more, and the test fails:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt; sanity-lnet test_241: @@@@@@ FAIL: Expected LND timeout 51
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The tunable is in fact set correctly. The same run shows:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;            lnd tunables:
                  conns_per_peer: 1
                  timeout: 51
                  tos: -1
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So this is a defect in the test helper, not in the LND timeout plumbing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_310 uses the same helper but configures all interfaces via lnet configure, so it passes today only because the count happens to equal ${#INTERFACES&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;@&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;}.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproduced on a 3-node rocky9 cluster whose LNet net runs on two interfaces (eth1, eth2).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Suggested fix: derive the expected count from the NIs actually configured on ${NETTYPE} rather than from ${INTERFACES&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;@&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;}.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
